  "euroleague_licenses_overview": {
    "description": "The main difference between FIBA Europe and modern Euroleague (since 2000) has been guaranteed participation via licenses. Initially 3-year A-licenses were used (13 in 2009, 14 in 2012). In 2015, 11 clubs signed long-term licenses until 2026 becoming shareholders. In 2021–22, ASVEL and Bayern Munich brought the shareholder count to 13.",
